blocks.en:
Figure 15 shows the median number of interaction steps per model across all three benchmarks.
The relationship between model capability and step efficiency is benchmark-dependent:
on ALFWorld, GPT-OSS-20B requires a median of 50 steps while most other models cluster around 15–18;
on WebShop, Qwen3-235B and Qwen3-Coder-30B are the most step-efficient (median 5 steps);
on WorkArena, all models converge to 5–10 steps.
These patterns confirm that planning capability—not raw inference speed—is the primary driver of episode cost in agentic settings.

blocks.zh:
图15显示所有三个基准每个模型的相互作用步骤的中位数。
模型能力和步效率之间的关系取决于基准:
在ALFWorld上,GPT-OSS-20B需要50步的中位数,而大多数其他模型则在15-18左右集群;
在WebShop上,Qune3-235B和Qune3-Coder-30B是最高效的一步(中间5步);
在WorkArena上,所有模型都汇合到5–10步骤.
这些模式证实,规划能力——而不是原始推论速度——是代理环境下的插曲成本的主要驱动因素。
